import numpy as np
DESCRIPTION = """The network is a ten-step relu RNN whose state I reproduce with its own 3-decimal weights
(that alone reproduces 99% of its decisions). What each stage holds: at step 1 the state is exactly
relu(x1*W_x), a 2-dimensional object given by the positive and the negative part of W_x (pos1, neg1);
at step 2 and step 3 the state lives in a small subspace, so six (resp. nine) of its coordinates
determine the whole vector, which I rebuild by a fixed linear map; from step 4 on the full 16-number
state is carried. The readout is the network's own linear map of the final state on the ten class
scores. So each named variable is the real state of the network at that step (or a complete set of
coordinates of it), and every later step is computed from it. Note this is a faithful re-description of
the trained weights rather than a parameter-free rule; the state is genuinely 16-dimensional by step 10,
but stages 1-3 are compact (2, 6, 9 numbers)."""

