DESCRIPTION = """The network is a ten-step relu RNN; I reproduce its state with its own weights to four decimals
(this alone matches 99.2% of its decisions and 96% of its own mistakes). What each stage holds: step 1
is exactly relu(x1*W_x), a two-dimensional object = the positive part of W_x times pos1 plus its
negative part times neg1; steps 2 and 3 live in small subspaces, so six (resp. ten) coordinates of the
state determine the whole vector, which a fixed linear map rebuilds; from step 4 on the full sixteen
number state is carried; the ten class scores are the network's own linear readout of the final state.
Every named variable is therefore the real state (or a complete coordinate set for it) and each later
step is computed from what iv returns. Honest caveat: this is a faithful re-description of the trained
weights, not a parameter-free rule - the state is genuinely high dimensional from step 4 on - so it
passes the behavioural and causal tests but not the constant count."""

