import numpy as np
DESCRIPTION = """The network computes the position of the second largest of the ten values, but
not symbolically: after the first step the state is a dense 16-vector and the recurrent map
h -> relu(x_t*W_x + h@W_h) is a full-rank 16x16 matrix with no low-rank, sparse or repeated
structure, so the trajectory is carried in full. Step 1 is exactly 2-dimensional:
h1 = x1^+ * max(W_x,0) + x1^- * max(-W_x,0), so the two numbers x1^+ and x1^- are named at h1.
At h2 only 6 numbers and at h3 only 10 numbers are needed (the reachable state stays nearly
inside a low-dimensional subspace early on); they are the coordinates v2 = (h2-mu2)@U2 and
v3 = (h3-mu3)@U3 and the state is rebuilt affinely from them. From h4 on the whole 16-vector is
named and passed on. The readout uses only the nine class differences W_o[:,c]-W_o[:,9] plus a
zero tenth column, which leaves the argmax unchanged."""
