position of the second largest of the ten inputs (95% agreement; the rest are near-ties). The state after step 1
is exactly 2-dimensional: h1 = pos1*max(W_x,0) + neg1*max(-W_x,0), pos1 = x1^+, neg1 = x1^-.
At step 2 only the seven units that the new input and the two step-1 quantities drive are named; at step 3 ten
coordinates; from step 4 on the whole 16-vector state is carried and the same one-step rule rebuilds each site
from the previous site's state. Units 0,2,3,5,10..15 have almost no input weight and only integrate the state;
units 4 and 1,6,7,8 have large input weights of opposite sign, so |x_t| enters through two opposing groups.
The readout takes ten linear scores from h_10."""

